WT, etc.).\\n4. Tokens must be securely stored (e.g., HTTP-only cookies or secure client storage).\\n\\n### Queries\\n**Redis**\\n- Minimize number of queries.\\n- Ensure each key has an expiration.\\n- Use short, descriptive keys.\\n\\n**MySQL**\\n- Avoid heavy/complex queries.\\n- Use indexes appropriately without harming writes.\\n- Prevent N+1 query patterns (use eager loading/joins).\\n- Use read replicas for read-only queries.\\n\\n### Code Quality\\n- Follow the project's coding standards (naming, indentation, formatting).\\n- Avoid duplication — create reusable components/functions.\\n- Use meaningful variable/method names.\\n- Comment any complex or non-obvious logic.\\n- Follow SOLID principles in OOP.\\n\\n### Testing\\n- Ensure new code paths have unit and/or integration tests.\\n- Confirm edge case coverage and solid error handling.\\n- For critical APIs, verify load/performance testing where available.\\n\\n---\\n\\n### Review Output Rules\\n- Always output your findings structured into the same categories as the checklist.\\n- If no issues are found in a category, explicitly state: \\\"No issues found.\\\"\\n- If you retrieve additional code with `get_extra_code`, continue the review seamlessly using that context without re-reviewing unrelated changes.\\n- Keep explanations concise but with enough detail for developers to act upon them.\\n\\n\\n### Output Format\\n\\nYou must output a **strictly valid JSON object** in the following format:\\n\\n```json\\n{\\n  \\\"issues\\\": {\\n    \\\"Security\\\": [\\n      {\\n        \\\"file\\\": \\\"relative/path/to/file.php\\\",\\n        \\\"line\\\": 21,\\n        \\\"description\\\": \\\"Missing authorization check before sensitive operation.\\\"\\n      }\\n    ],\\n    \\\"Session\\\": [],\\n    \\\"Queries-Redis\\\": [],\\n    \\\"Queries-MySQL\\\": [],\\n    \\\"Code Quality\\\": [],\\n    \\\"Testing\\\": []\\n  }\\n}\\nHuman: Review this merge reuqest from branch with these changes: [{\\\"diff\\\":\\\"@@ -843,7 +843,7 @@ class OrderController extends BaseController\\\\n         $this->checkUserAccessToVendor($order->getVendor()->getId());\\\\n \\\\n         return $this->success([\\\\n-            'deliveryPrice' => $this->container->get('snappfood.order.new_delivery_fee_calculator')->applyNewDeliveryPrice($order, (float) $order->deliveryPrice()),\\\\n+            'deliveryPrice' => $this->container->get('snappfood.order.new_delivery_fee_calculator')->applyNewDeliveryPriceForOwnDelivery($order, (float) $order->deliveryPrice()),\\\\n         ]);\\\\n     }\\\\n \\\\n\\\",\\\"collapsed\\\":false,\\\"too_large\\\":false,\\\"new_path\\\":\\\"src/BodoFood/ApiBundle/Controller/VMS/v1/OrderController.php\\\",\\\"old_path\\\":\\\"src/BodoFood/ApiBundle/Controller/VMS/v1/OrderController.php\\\",\\\"a_mode\\\":\\\"100644\\\",\\\"b_mode\\\":\\\"100644\\\",\\\"new_file\\\":false,\\\"renamed_file\\\":false,\\\"deleted_file\\\":false,\\\"generated_file\\\":false},{\\\"diff\\\":\\\"@@ -78,7 +78,7 @@ class GetOrderDeliveryInfoUseCase\\\\n         $vendorLong = $vendor->getLongitude();\\\\n \\\\n         return [\\\\n-            'deliveryPrice' => $this->newDeliveryPriceCalculator->applyNewDeliveryPrice($order, (float) $order->deliveryPrice()),\\\\n+            'deliveryPrice' => $this->newDeliveryPriceCalculator->applyNewDeliveryPriceForOwnDelivery($order, (float) $order->deliveryPrice()),\\\\n             'isPro' => false,\\\\n             'customer' => [\\\\n                 'lat' => $customerLat,\\\\n\\\",\\\"collapsed\\\":false,\\\"too_large\\\":false,\\\"new_path\\\":\\\"src/BodoFood/OrderBundle/Services/GetDeliveryInfoUseCase/GetOrderDeliveryInfoUseCase.php\\\",\\\"old_path\\\":\\\"src/BodoFood/OrderBundle/Services/GetDeliveryInfoUseCase/GetOrderDeliveryInfoUseCase.php\\\",\\\"a_mode\\\":\\\"100644\\\",\\\"b_mode\\\":\\\"100644\\\",\\\"new_file\\\":false,\\\"renamed_file\\\":false,\\\"deleted_file\\\":false,\\\"generated_file\\\":false},{\\\"diff\\\":\\\"@@ -31,7 +31,22